# Public host name pointing (A record) at the server. Caddy obtains the TLS certificate automatically.
DOMAIN=subs.example.com
# The address the server gives out in links and to the apps (defaults to https://$DOMAIN).
#BASE_URL=https://subs.example.com
# Tencent Cloud keys. The apps never receive them: live audio is relayed through this server (实时语音识别 for the
# default split pipeline, 实时语音翻译 for the combined one) and uploads use 录音文件识别.
TENCENT_APPID=
TENCENT_SECRET_ID=
TENCENT_SECRET_KEY=
# Which Tencent edge the relay speaks to: cn (Guangzhou, the default: the mainland rate, right while the people
# speaking are in mainland China) | auto (a mainland edge found by DNS) | system (whatever the system resolver
# answers — from a server abroad an overseas edge, billed as 跨境 at about twice the price).
#TENCENT_EDGE=cn
# Translation of uploads: TokenHub API key (console.cloud.tencent.com/tokenhub/apikey). Without it the server
# falls back to the standalone Hunyuan API with the keys above, which Tencent shuts down on 2026-09-30.
TOKENHUB_API_KEY=
# hy-mt2-pro (default, flagship) | hy-mt2-plus | hy-mt2-lite
#TRANSLATION_MODEL=hy-mt2-pro
# Alibaba 百炼 API key (bailian.console.aliyun.com › API-Key, 华北2（北京）): uploads in Japanese are recognised with
# fun-asr there, which hears about twice what Tencent's 16k_ja does. Without it every language stays with Tencent.
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=
MAX_UPLOAD_GB=8
# Dashboard usage card. The keys above can already read usage (asr:GetUsageByDate). Tencent has no API for a resource
# pack's remaining quota, so to show what is left of the 实时语音翻译 pack tell the server what was bought:
# hours@purchase-date. TENCENT_PACK_COVERS=all counts file recognition against the pack too (default: live only).
#TENCENT_PACK=32h@2026-08-01
#TENCENT_PACK_COVERS=live
# Account balance on the dashboard needs a finance permission (billing:DescribeAccountBalance; preset
# QcloudFinanceBillReadOnlyAccess). Give it to a separate API key so the speech key cannot read the account.
# Optional.
#TENCENT_BILLING_SECRET_ID=
#TENCENT_BILLING_SECRET_KEY=
# Accounts: closed (only `node server/cli.js add-user` creates accounts; default) | invite (sign-up with a code from
# `node server/cli.js add-invite`) | open (anyone can sign up). Change and restart; nothing else needs rebuilding.
SIGNUP_MODE=closed
# Who administers the server (the Team page). Without it the first account becomes administrator.
#ADMIN_EMAIL=
# Notifications for "request an account" from the website, as an email from your own mailbox. iCloud:
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.mail.me.com SMTP_PORT=587 SMTP_USER=you@icloud.com SMTP_PASS=<app-specific password from
# account.apple.com>. Gmail: smtp.gmail.com / 587 / your address / an app password. Verify with
# `docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml --env-file deploy/.env exec app node server/cli.js test-mail`.
#SMTP_HOST=
#SMTP_PORT=587
#SMTP_USER=
#SMTP_PASS=
#MAIL_FROM=
#NOTIFY_EMAIL=
# And/or a chat webhook (Discord or Slack incoming webhook URL).
#REQUEST_WEBHOOK_URL=
